# Installation

{{ project_name }} is installed as a **Blender extension**: a zip holding the add-on and
the wheels of the Python packages it needs, so nothing is installed into Blender's own
Python and nothing is downloaded when Blender installs it.

## Requirements

- Blender 4.2 or newer.
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and `make`, to build the extension from source.

## 1. Tell the build where Blender is

Create a `.env` file in the project root (or `~/.config/blender-ci.env`):

```sh
BLENDER=/Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender
```

| Variable | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `BLENDER` | The Blender executable. Used to build the zip, validate the manifest and install. |

The file is looked up in this order: `BLENDER_CI_ENV_FILE`, `./.env`,
`~/.config/blender-ci.env`.

## 2. Install

```sh
make install
```

| Target | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `make extension` | Builds `dist/{{ package_slug }}-<version>.zip`: wheels of this package and of its locked dependencies plus the extension, packed by Blender. |
| `make install` | Builds the zip, then installs it in the `user_default` repository and enables it. |
| `make uninstall` | Disables and removes it. |
| `make validate` | Checks `extension/blender_manifest.toml` with Blender. |

### Without make

Build the zip with `make extension`, then in Blender use **Edit > Preferences > Get
Extensions**, the arrow menu (top right) and **Install from Disk**.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Check |
| --- | --- |
| `Set BLENDER in ...` | The env file is missing or does not define `BLENDER`. |
| `blender_manifest.toml is at version X, VERSION says Y` | Run `make update-version` and set the same version in the manifest. |
| A dependency is not bundled | One zip serves every platform, so dependencies must be pure Python wheels. |
| Old behavior after pulling changes | Run `make install` again. |
